1</label><caption><p>Questionnaire regarding pet ownership and exposure modality. The questionnaire was modified from a previous report by Liccardi et al.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B7">7</xref></p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-5-295-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>The sensitization rate of common inhalant allergens in the study subjects. Dp, <italic>Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus</italic>; Df, <italic>Dermatophagoides farinae</italic>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-5-295-g002"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Clinical characteristics of subjects sensitized to each animal allergen</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-5-295-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>'Others' includes hamster, chicken, cows, and birds. <sup>&#x02020;</sup>Chronic cough excludes asthma and allergic rhinitis as causative diseases of chronic cough.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Modality of exposure to each animal</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-5-295-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.0001 using chi-square tests between direct and indirect, and between direct and no exposure.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Independent risk factors for sensitization to each animal allergen</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="aair-5-295-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>Indicates a <italic>P</italic> value of 0.05 or less. OR, odds ratio; CI, confidence interval; Binary logistic regression analyses were performed controlling for age and sex as covariates.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>